\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par I urge you to take the unusual step of putting the pr
otection of public health over that of industrial profits.  Once these plants are set loose in the environment, everyone in our country becomes a guinea pig with no control over the results.  Prevention is worth an ounce of cure under these circumstances.

\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Kathy Ruopp
\par 9631 S Vanderpoel
\par Chicago, IL 60643
\par 
\par 
