\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Disregard these form letters from organic food interests
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Please disregard this bull-crap. These are organic food activists trying to scare us into eating less than average f
ood derived from crops that have been fertilized with waste from cows, pigs, chickens and humans. For goodness sakes, these folks have killed countless people with their propaganda. 
\par 
\par Enough is enough. Go Ventria!
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Rayford Minrada
\par 4720 Fiftieth Avenue
\par Wichita, KS 66056
\par 
\par 
