\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: "pharma" crops threaten environmental contamination
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par As you know, "pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especia
lly in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. This potentially  risks  human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination.  Neither the USDA nor b
iotechnology companies have proven trustworthy to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I strongly urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Sharon Handy
\par 306 James SE
\par Grand Rapids, MI 49503
\par 
\par 
