\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 6130 s.e. 18th ave , portland, OR 97202 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 22, 2007   8:37 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep GE Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par We know that "Pharma" and industrial food crops contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in to
rnado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses risks to human health, threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination, and denies us the basic right o
f
 knowing what we are buying when we grocery shop. A macarobiotic diet of whole, organic foods has helped me to beat cancer---understandably, I want to know what I'm eating! Monsanto's concern is not for our safety, but for the profits it makes by experime
nting on us. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I adamantly oppose USDA approval of this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops 
and support a ban on this practice altogether. Remember when we were told that DDT was safe? My grandfather bathed his tomatoes in it; my type of cancer has been conclusively linked to DDT exposure. Let's not continue to experiment in this way with the li
ves of our children and grandchildren---for they will surely be impacted most by these GE experiments.
\par 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par shannon moore
\par 6130 s.e. 18th ave
\par portland, OR 97202
\par 
\par 
