\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par It's not even a question of IF other crops will be contaminated by the bio-engineered ones, it's a matter of WHEN.
\par 
\par Stop allowing human beings to be used as unwitting, unwilling test subjects for this untested, potentially disastrous technology.
\par 
\par The USDA does not exist to promote corporate interests over the interests of American citizens.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par John Domingue
\par 3246 S. Corona
\par Englewood, CO 80113
\par 
