\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par genetically modified food in general has an negative impact to human health because it is against nature. this is a fact that has been prouved by an indipend
ent laboratory in siena, italy. animals fed with genmodified food showed changings of the organs and less enzymes inside their stomach. curiously, the government of berlusconi has stopped this scientific project. showing that gentechnology is unhealthy se
ems to be "economically incorrect". but what is the more important: business or the health of humans?
\par open growing so-called "pharma" food can and will contaminate neighboring fields, especialls when there are tornados. this contamination poses serious risks to humans, like for example immunification against medicaments.
\par further, experience has prouved that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination. how could they? nature is not controllable and we shouldn't play go
d, because that has bad consequences.for us and for the nature that we depend on. an example: because in malaysia there are so many genmodified plants, people must now overtake the role of beens to fertilisize fruit trees and other plants. otherwise the e
cological sytem would collapse. and all this because people wanted comfortable agriculture. is it comfortable and economic when peolpe have to overtake the role of animals?
\par technology is good, but not allways. there are ethical limits that should be respected.
\par we should take more care about this planet, because the world we build right now is the world our children and grandchildren have to live in.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny the application by ventria bioscience to grow this drug-producing rice in kansas and also all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.

\par 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Nina Kass
\par 30, rue Michel Gehrend
\par /
\par Luxembourg L-1619
\par 
\par 
\par 
