\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 16, 2007   5:41 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par I oppose the approval of the application by Ventria to grow genetically modified rice in an outdoor field in Kansas. Studies and anecdotal reports illustrate examples of wind-caused contamination at considerable (almost 10
,000 feet) distances. A windy and tornado-prone area such as Kansas could present a larger danger of wind-borne contamination which could pose unacceptable risks to neighboring farmers and human health. I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applicati
ons for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Matthew Roman
\par 69 Baldwin St #11
\par Johnson City, NY 13790-2140
\par 
\par 
