\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 Kathleen Kite-Powell
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 4284 Glenlake Drive , Kennesaw, GA 30144 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 15, 2007   1:52 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Please Prevent Drugs From Reaching Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par I believe that pharmaceutical-producing food crops are a very bad idea to grow outdoors. Even indoors, there is a risk of contaminatin
g our food crops. It would be better if non-food crops were grown indoors and processed safely for these compounds. More specifically, it might be a good idea to disallow food crops with pharmaceuticals to be produced in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds 
o
r a direct hit to a closed facility could end up blowing pharma rice seeds into neighboring food crop fields, where they might be harvested together and thus threaten the food supply. Contamination could definitely pose serious risks to human health eithe
r
 to all or parts of our consumer population, and threaten farmers who may be held liable for contamination. According to the Union of Concerned Scientists, experience has already shown that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to pr
event contamination. Yet it is a job that the USDA should be doing with great care.
\par 
\par As a concerned ex-research scientist and medical writer, I emphatically urge the USDA to consider denying this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmace
utical and industrial food crops; thus, instituting a ban on this practice altogether, so that the US population can remain safe. It would be a terrible shame for you to find out after the fact that you had allowed a practice that had truly harmed or kill
ed consumers! Please, lets keep that sort of item out of the news. A little forethought and prevention can go a long way.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Kathleen Kite-Powell
\par 4284 Glenlake Drive
\par Kennesaw, GA 30144
\par 
\par 
