\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 sonia skakich
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 15011 e arkansas dr , aurora, CO 80012 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 14, 2007   8:24 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Unacceptable risks:food and seed supply
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma ric
e seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies h
ave historically successfully prevented event contamination, nor would such prevention even be possible.
\par 
\par Further, the crop and soil contamination of the larger food supply poses the following additional risks:
\par -contamination of other crops, with unknown/un
researched health impact -contamination of other crops adding invisible drug burden to the population, with potential for negative drug interactions, negative impacts on vulnerable populations -contamination of seed supply -unknown effects on soil nutrien
t
s, soil bacteria, other species of animals,  environmental interactions Each of these are serious issues in and of themselves, with many complex unknowns, but together, these issues indicate unacceptable levels of risk to our agriculture, our population, 
our seed supply, and our environment.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par sonia skakich
\par 15011 e arkansas dr
\par aurora, CO 80012
\par 
\par 
