\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--
especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contami
nation. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par What is feared here has already happened with crops engineered to resist Round-Up. I am not surprised at "Pharma" wishing to proceed as if nothing happened. But, I am distressed, to say the least, that the USDA has not l
earned a lesson. And, distressed that the USDA does not value our health nor work to protect the small farmers who will end up caught up in "Pharma's" pursuit of profits when the genetically altered crops show up in other farm fields, as they certainly wi
ll.
\par 
\par Come on!!!! Behave responsibly.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Louis Harris, Jr.
\par 1002 Abington Rd.
\par Cherry Hill, NJ 08034
\par 
\par 
