\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 Mark Nanny
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 1815 Lakehurst Drive , Norman, OK 73071 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 13, 2007   1:50 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par As an environmental chemistry professor and researcher, I certainly va
lue the benefits of biotechnology and how its advances can solve agricultural, environmental, and pharmaceutical challenges.  However, I am greatly concerned about genetically engineering food crops to express drugs and/or human enzymes.  The risk of cros
s
-pollination to crops intended for human and animal consumption is practically a certainity. Added to the fact that our food crops are limited in the number of species we use, contamination of our monoculture food crops would be a great global catastrophe
.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely, Dr. Mark A. Nanny Associate Professor, Enviromental Chemistry University of Oklahoma
\par 
\par 202 West Boyd Street, Room 334 Norman, OK 73019
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Mark Nanny
\par 1815 Lakehurst Drive
\par Norman, OK 73071
\par 
\par 
