\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par I know these sorts of crops are grown in Michigan, where I live. I know which counties these crops are grown in
. However, I do not know, nor am I ALLOWED to know exactly where in the county, or what kind of drug or drug producing crop is growing.  In addition to being discomforted by this knowledge, I am angered that this practice, and the secrecy has been allowed
.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses p
otentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Stephanie Gerdan
\par 10838 Beebe Hwy
\par Tipton, MI 49287
\par 
