\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\fs20\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 Deb Sparrow
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 1715 S. La Rosa , Tempe, AZ 85281 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 12, 2007   4:45 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Safe Food Supply
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Genetically engineered plants have already spread to wild ones and the consequences are serious.  We must protect the food supply and heavily regulate pharmaceutical and industrial agriculture.
\par 
\par Grasses share pollen and genes very easily.
\par Grass grown with roundup ready genes will make it even more difficult to prevent fire in the west.  Roundup is a very valuable tool in fire prevention.  This herbicide is used widely in weed management and if it looses it's impact on grasse
s, fighting fires will be even more costly.  It is already hard enough in our water-starved western states.
\par 
\par Rice is also a grass and as stated above, grasses share genes very effectively.  Growing rice with human genes for drug production outdoors is terrificly risky.
\par 
\par Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. 
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Deb Sparrow
\par 1715 S. La Rosa
\par Tempe, AZ 85281
\par 
\par 
