\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Insist on effective oversight for pharma crops
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. 
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops unless there is effective oversight on the conta
mination issue. Certainly, these crops have dramatic potential to aid in responsible drug produciton but I believe the contamination issue poses a more serious risk under the current applications than the potential benefits.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par 
\par Bruce Rawlinson 13279 NE 183rd St.
\par Woodinville, WA 98072 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Bruce Rawlinson
\par 13279 NE 183RD ST
