\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 904-A Rio Grande St. , Austin, TX 78701-2222 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 12, 2007   4:06 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par [Further down are several research papers related to this subject and the problems with GM/GE modified crops and the human food supply.]
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of c
orn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contaminati
on.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par There is much research available on the web demonstrating beyond-a-shadow-of
-doubt that trangenic DNA is different from natural DNA and is more likely to spread by horizontal gene transfer and recombination, both by design and otherwise. I hope you will refute these point by point.
\par 
\par Go here http://www.i-sis.org.uk/secretGMcrops.php
\par 
\par to read the article by Dr. Mae-Wan Ho, entitled -- The Best Kept Secret of GM Crops by the Institute of Sience in Society [ISIS].
\par [the above article is also available here --in case the link has been removed-- http://www.biotech-info.net/best_secret.html ]
\par 
\par Here is another research report on the lateral transmission of genes in biosystems for your review--
\par 
\par Information on the Lateral Transmission of Genes in Biosystems
\par 
\par http://64.233.167.104/search?q=cache:glpa_v1xwYEJ:www.yvm.net/vme/hgt/TrendsInGeneticspp1-4yr1986.PDF+cross+species+transmission+of+genes&hl=en
\par 
\par Consequently, I am writing to voice a "NO" request to not approve this application for 3200 acres of G/M (rice or other crop) production by Ventria Bioscience or any other GM/GE company until furt
her research and tests have been proven to refute the very dangerous impact of GM & GE foods on the human food supply and food chain.
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Stan Shaw
\par 904-A Rio Grande St.
\par Austin, TX 78701-2222
\par 
\par 
