\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Just Because You're "Sequenced" a Gene
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Does NOT mean you understand it, or everything it does.  Remember the unintended consequences of even simple drugs like Thalidomide.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food cro
ps will contaminate the entire food supply when winds blow gene-gineered seeds into neighboring fields. Contamination poses serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USD
A nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par D. H. Strong
\par Bismark Road
\par COCOA, FL 32927
