\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are not only likely to 
contaminate the food supply, they will without a doubt if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risk
s to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA (you guys) nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications
 for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether. Don't you guys get it?  Genetic pollution is not a good thing at all!!  Why is that not evident to the USDA? One would think that you a
re nothing but corporate stooges with way you rubber stamp and approve such dangerous and precedent setting practices. Do your jobs and protect our health and environment from such asinine practices.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par jonathan buckmaster
\par p.o. box 773
\par arcata, CA 95518
\par 
\par 
