\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 Elizabeth Skipper
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 1 Melendy Hollow , Amherst, NH 03031 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 11, 2007   5:12 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Wherever GMO crops have been grown, it has been shown that they have spread and contaminated their non-GMO neighbors.  It is impossible, especially outdoors, to keep any type of crop contained.  There are too many ways for them to spread and proprogate.  

\par 
\par I, as well as the majority of consumers when asked, oppose the genetic engineering of our food supply.  The technology is new and unproven, and presents an unacceptable risk to life forms which have taken millions of years to develop.
\par 
\par I urgently request the USDA to deny this application, as well as all others, for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops.   In fact, I believe this practice should be banned in its entirety. 
\par 
\par We have already loosed genetically engineered material into the environment, to what effect remains to be seen.  Let us not compound the problem further, for the gain of commercial enterprise.  
\par 
\par The solution to children with diarrhea and related ailments is clean water, a clean environment, and sufficient high-quality food, NOT genetically engineered rice!
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Elizabeth Skipper
\par 1 Melendy Hollow
\par Amherst, NH 03031
\par 
\par 
