\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in torn
ado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience
 shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par GMO crops have not been proven safe, far from it, but pharmaceutical GMO crops are another order of magnitude altogether.  The USDA is charged with protecting agriculture and the American public health.  It is doing neither.  What a trave
sty - the US government is fast-tracking the interests of Ventria at the expense of American citizens.  As a very wise Native American chief once said, "We should consider all of our decisions in terms of the next seven generations."  Obviously, the USDA 
is not even considering the well-being of the NEXT generation.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Paulette Licht
\par 212 Half Mile Road
\par North Haven, CT, CT 06473-4112
\par 
