\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 11, 2007   3:50 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par I purchase only organic fruits and vegetables for the sole purpose of wantin
g to eat pure and natural foods free of pesticides and Genetic Modification. I am exasperated that myself and my friends will no longer be able to know that that these foods are safe. If Pharma crops are grown outdoors, they are likely to contaminate our 
food supply -- especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat.
\par 
\par It is our human right to be healthy, happy and whole.
\par 
\par Let us deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharma crops.
\par 
\par Thank you.
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Pam Nobuto
\par 11042 Otsego St.
\par N Hollywood, CA 91601
\par 
\par 
