\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par I am totally opposd to allowing genetically engineered crops to be grown outdoors where it is virtually impossib
le to contain them.  You know and I know it cannot be done.  And we do not know the long-term or "unintended" effects of such genetically modified material. 
\par 
\par You risk our food supply!  And you risk the livelihoods of food crop farmers.  And especially for "Pharma" crops?
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Teresa Hopkins
\par 1826 1st St
\par Kirkland, WA 98033
