\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 14831 Ronda Drive , San Jose, CA 95124-5114 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 11, 2007   12:00 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par      Sir, I have been a gardener all my adult life, close to 50 years.  Nothing in my experience suggests any rationale for the myth that open-grown farmcrops can be contained.  I certainly can'
t do it on my own ground, and I'm only working a city lot.  This experiment is at hideous risk to mankind because once these genes escape, there's no calling them back..Please, sir, don't gamble with my children's world.
\par     
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Jeanne Barber
\par 14831 Ronda Drive
\par San Jose, CA 95124-5114
\par 
\par 
