\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Genetically Modified Rice
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par The potential use of rice modified with human genes is not only a disgusting use of science, but a danger to our food supply.  
\par 
\par The USDA needs to start doing its job to protect American consumers.  Please do not allow Ventria Bioscience to conduct this unnecessary experiment on our food supply.  People are not guinea pigs.  
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Joseph Charles
\par 36 Gramercy Park East
\par Apt 7E
\par New York, NY 10003
\par 
\par 
