\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keed Drugs and GMOs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops 
are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human he
alth and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. History shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of 
pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether. I also urge you to ban the cultivation of all other GMO crops entirely, as most other developed countires in the world have already done. More and more studies ar
e showing that GMO foods are detrimental to human health. If the USA is supposed to be the "world leader" then why are we always the last ones to clean up our act?
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Peter Veits
\par 6140 Clinton Ave
\par Minneapolis, MN 55419
\par 
