\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 46 Morgan Ave , Oneonta, NY 13820 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 10, 2007   4:23 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par I am very con
cerned that "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors. I am especially concerned about growing them in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of co
rn, soybeans, or wheat. 
\par 
\par How can the profits of the few be put before the well being of the many? Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither th
e USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination. It is like opening Pandora's box - let's prevent the chaos from being unleashed.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Colleen Blacklock
\par 46 Morgan Ave
\par Oneonta, NY 13820
\par 
\par 
