\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "P
harma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses pote
ntially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination.
\par 
\par This can also destroy organic crops that could be unintentionally exposed to these GE crops. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par Doesn't the fact that Europe has banned GE crops and does not want to trade for our crops that have been altered in ways that could prove very harmful down the road, mean anything to you. Why do you allow you
rself to be bought off by Big Agri, which cares nothing for our health and well being, and only about profits. You are a US agency to protect the people of this country, not to cow-tow to big business.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Laura Sullivan
\par 4789 Drayton Harbor Rd
\par Blaine, WA 98230
\par 
\par 
