\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Has Ventria Bioscience or any other company learned how to control the wind?
\par 
\par If not,"Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seed
s into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health.  It also threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies c
an be trusted, whatever their good intentions, to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par We urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
