\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 10, 2007   4:18 AM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination.  Experience shows biotechnology companies cannot be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par Ventria BioScience's manufacturing processes, using human genes to produce lactoferrin, lysozyme and serumalbumin to be used in the production of foods such as 
yogurt, granola bars, and replacement meals is revolting, and a betrayal of the public's trust.  Surely you wouldn't allow your family to consume such a vile invention!
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par Sincerely, Valerie J Harding.
\par 515 N. Lincoln Ave. Clearwater, Florida, 33755
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Valerie Harding
\par 515 N. Lincoln Ave.
\par Cleatwater, FL 33755
\par 
