\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easi
ly blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotech
nology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par Moreover, I refuse to buy food that has been genetically engineered, PERIOD. And with human genes, is just crazy. Stop playing with our food! 
\par 
\par I strongly urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Teri Travis
\par 9736 Sand Pt Wy NE
\par Seattle, WA 98115
\par 
\par 
