\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par History has shown these crops contaminate other, natural crops. Those of us who wish to eat genetically natural food are beign deprived of our right to do so. We are being force fed ge contamination.
\par 
\par I am from Kansas. My family still lives there. I do not want my beloved state contaminated with g e produced crops! 
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par And while you are at it please introduce a bill for mandatory labeling of all genetically modified foods! Science has shown they pose a dangerous threat to health and well being.
\par Thank you.
\par 
\par Terrence M. Schenk 1000 N. 4th St.
\par Fairfield, IA   52557
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Terry Schenk
\par 1000 N 4th St
\par Fairfield, IA 52557
\par 
