\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 Carol Cates
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 10509 Vernon Rd. , Lake Stevens, WA 98258 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 9, 2007   8:48 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Grow No Drugs in Our Food!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par There are no areas where wind does 
not blow at least once in a while.  That is one way that food crops may be contaminated by genetically-engineered crops which may be many, many miles away.  Once food crops are contaminated, we lose not only that season's crops, but it is very possible th
at we lose those crops forever.  There is no reason for drugs to be grown outdoors via genetically modified plants especially when all the risks are weighed.
\par 
\par Contamination from outdoor-grown, genetically-engineered/modified plants is inevitable.  Please consider putting a ban on this practice as soon as possible rather than putting our food supply in danger needlessly.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Carol Cates
\par 10509 Vernon Rd.
\par Lake Stevens, WA 98258
\par 
\par 
