\par  
\par 
\par Subject: No "Pharma Crops" in U.S. Food Supply---Protect U.S. Public Health!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par I'm a registered voter and a concerned citizen in the Los Angeles area, and I worry that the U.S. and worldwide food security will be threatened by this breach of pharamceutical-producing crops in the U.S.:
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily
 blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechno
logy companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Jo-Shing Yang
\par P.O. Box 189326
\par Sacramento, CA 95818
\par 
\par 
