\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Such genetically engineered food crops will contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, so
ybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.

\par 
\par App
roving such practices is denying the right of concerned consumers to avoid genetically engineered foods.  I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on 
this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Erbin Crowell
\par 1245 Reynolds Rd.
\par Chepachet, RI 02814
