\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are like
ly to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and
 threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Growing genetically altered crops in the open air, ensuring contamination of people and crops around it, is irresponsible beyond belief!!
\par If our government agencies ca
nnot control such practices and protect the people, who can we turn to?  I am tired of mega-companies using the american public as guinea pigs for testing their new creations.... The standard example is, of course, DDT... which we eventually got off the m
arket, then the less than ethical American Corporations sold it overseas and now we can still ingest it in imported produce.
\par  Please put a stop NOW to arrogant an impractical actions of big business.  That is why our founding fathers and their descendents created oversight agencies.  To OVERSEE, not AVERT ONE'S SIGHT!
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par cheri warzecha
\par 220 main st
\par new hartford, CT 06057
\par 
\par 
