\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par There has already been far too much contamination through wind-blown pollination of normal food crops by allowing outdoors planting of geneticlly engineered crops.
\par 
\par Please STOP "Pharma" and industrial food crops being grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, 
or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks THAT I DO NOT WANT YOU TO TAKE and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. 
\par 
\par Experience shows that  biotechnology companies can NOT be trusted to prevent contamination.   CAN YOU?
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par susan Curry
\par 316 Edgewood Dr.
\par Ambler, PA 19002-4305
