\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par The long-term damage and dangers implicit to the certain spread of genetic material from these crops from the proposed area far outweigh any public good Ventria Bioscience could possibly achieve in this venture. 
\par 
\par As a concerned citizen, one who was born and raised in the neighboring state of Colorado, I urge you to deny their application and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Loren Drummond
\par 1319 Maryland Ave. NE
\par Washington, DC 20002
\par 
\par 
