\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 9, 2007   1:54 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par I am trying
 to eat healthy food, as are many others. For that reason, I strongly object to outdoor ?pharming? of food crops, which are likely to contaminate the food supply. In tornado-prone Kansas, particularly, winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighb
oring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. 
\par 
\par Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination, and yet this poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. 
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for OUTDOOR production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops. I also urge you to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Elizabeth Rogers
\par 310 Cenacle Rd.
\par Ronkonkoma, NY 11779-2203
\par 
\par 
