\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 5829 Central Ave , Bonita, CA 91902 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 9, 2007   11:34 AM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns, 
\par 
\par I would like to ask the USDA to deny not only this, but all applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical products in food crops.
\par First of all, we should keep all artificial ingredients out of our food supply, especially medicine to which we will not react when we really need it because we will be immune to it through previous exposure.
\par Second, it has been shown over and over again, how easily seeds can be wind blown from one field (and one species of crop) to another. And Kansas has its share of ?wind?. What about when the drugs
 produced in the rice field show up in other crops and people inadvertently eat it. Who will take the blame for the consequences?
\par The USDA is supposed to look out for the well being of the population, not for the already stuffed pocket book of big pharmaceutical groups. And that is what I expect it to do.
\par Sincerely, Ilse Taylor 5829 Central Av.
\par Bonita CA, 91902
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Ilse Taylor
\par 5829 Central Ave
\par Bonita, CA 91902
\par 
\par 
