\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\fs20\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 Rev. Larry Bernard, O.F.M.
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 St. Joseph Church PO Box 1000, Laguna, NM 87026 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   11:01 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Restrict genetically modified crops from outside growth
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par It is important to consider the overall health of our planetary home. It requires humility to a
ccept that we don't know the long-term consequences of creating genetically modified crops. It is wise, it is respectful, it is fitting and proper that such crop experiments be allowed only inside greenhouses. When planted outside they can contaminate oth
er crops and cause unknown consequences which may not be beneficial.
\par 
\par In Kansas winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. 
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and other genetically modified food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Rev. Larry Bernard, O.F.M.
\par St. Joseph Church
\par PO Box 1000
\par Laguna, NM 87026
\par 
\par 
