\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 3880 Stikes Drive, S.E. , Lacey, WA 98503 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   11:01 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Certainly, if "Pharma" and industrial food crops are grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat this is a serious problem. Contaminatio
n poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par We strongly urge the USDA to take steps NOW to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par This makes no sense.  Contamination must not occur, and it is your responsibility to take the steps to see that it does not occur.  Thanks.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Diane Williams
\par 3880 Stikes Drive, S.E.
\par Lacey, WA 98503
\par 
\par 
