\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where wind
s could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA
 nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Remember t
he accidental release of the hybrid Bee created from the European Honey Bee and the African Bee?  This one incident is still causing devastation throught South and North America. You cannot guarantee that this is safe for the people or the other spieces a
r
ound the area where this is to be tested. Why do Humans think that they can improve Nature when in fact we cannot!!!!!  If you don't believe me, then why do we have Killer Bees everywhere and our native Bees are dying off and disappearing.  We need people
 with common sense when it comes to making laws and making decisions that affect us all in the U.S. and also for the rest of the world!
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Loretta Thompson
\par 1782 Nisson Road  #74
\par Tustin, CA 92780
\par 
\par 
