\par  
\par 
\par Subject: NO Genetically Engineered Crops Grown in the Open Air!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Allowing genetically engineered crops and the so-called "Pharma Food" to be grown in the outdoors will contaminate neighboring fie
lds and additional crops grown near and far.  It will contaminate the food we eat!  It is simply irresponsible to allow agriculture companies who want to conduct this kind of experiment to contaminate our food supply.  Add to that the fact that Ventria is
 talking about growing this in Kansas, where winds are strong and tornados are not an uncommon occurance and you are, in essence, contaminating the other crops on purpose.  Is that what the plan is?  Because the outcome is inevitable.
\par 
\par I buy organic because
 I do not want to eat or serve genetically engineered food, I don't want bovine growth hormones in my dairy products.  And, I certainly don't want the government of the United States to take that choice away from me by making irresponsible choices such as
 this.
\par 
\par Contamination such as this poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Julianne Ramaker
\par 1375 NE Elk Court
\par Bend, OR 97701
\par 
\par 
