\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Always keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par My family and I do not want "Pharma" and industr
ial food crops.  We are very concerned about contamination to our food supply.  Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotec
hnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.  We must leave our food supply in its natural and healthy state - no engineered and manipulated food for us.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Mary Derstine
\par 14 Birch Road
\par Kinnelon, NJ 07405
