\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown out
doors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for 
contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par These crops have the potential to contaminate crops throughout North America and beyond. I urge you to be responsible in making decisions which affect the health of US citizens and your environment, as well as wor
ld citizens and the global environment. I urge you to be a responsible world leader and ban genetically engineered rice crops and GE crops generally.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Zoe Lambert
\par 4637 Arran Rd.
\par Courtenay, BC V9N 9S6
\par 
\par 
