\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   8:03 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par I am deeply concerned that our health and well-being is being sacrificed, due soley to a lack of intelligence and integrity on the part of certain powerful industries and their minions. Please take your best opportunity, which is now, to firmly direct the
 USDA toward it's only reason for being, that of overseeing the content and quality of food marketed in the USA, and making that information easily available to everyone.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown
 outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable 
for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Please do the right thing - you will be remembered for it in either case.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Yvette Sabin
\par P.O. Box 2375
\par Port Angeles, WA 98362
\par 
\par 
