\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   7:28 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornad
o-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience s
hows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par JOHN DIERIG
\par 610 Carrington Pl
\par #207
\par LOVELAND, OH 45140-8668
\par 
\par 
