\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par I urge, beg, and hope that you deeply consider the consequencies of genetically engineered food or drug products.  I truly believe that demons we are f
ighting now are the secrets that have escaped from laboratories around the world (bird flu, AIDS, flesh eating bacteria, etc.)
\par 
\par I understand the world is growing & business need to produce more food for everyone; however, this isn't the answer.  
\par 
\par More organic farms in the USA!  More organic everything!  Back to basics.  The USA doesn't produce anything but poison - DDT shipped to other countries; our crops sent to Europe, etc.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if
 grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held l
iable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Beth Martinez
\par 2410 S Holman Cir
\par Lakewood, CO 80228
\par 
\par 
