\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Please do not risk our children's future for this economic gain today. This is completely unethical. "Pharma" and industrial food crops will  contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors, winds will blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn
, soybeans, or wheat. 
\par 
\par Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who will be held liable for contamination. 
\par 
\par Experience with Monsanto engineered grains in Canada has shown that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can or will  prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely, Stephanie Simon 83 Spruce Street Warwick, RI 02886
