\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of
 corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par This is an issue of having the intelligence to understand that there are risks here that can affect the human population as a whole, you and your familes included. Take a moment and react with your brain, not your greed.
\par 
