\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\fs20\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 Debra Anderson
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 106 Darling Street , Bennington, VT 05201 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   6:33 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: It is Extremely Important to Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par It is completely unwise to allow outdoor growth of any genetically engineered, let alone drug producing plants.  It is not at all hard to imagine the wind blowing your seeds into fields growing food. What is the plan for mass contamin
ation if there is a tornado?  Don't tell me nothing bad will happen because I will not beleive you.  I eat from my organic garden as much as possible but when I do eat mass produced food I want it to be what you say it is.... safe.
\par I am a beekeeper.   I am
 desperately concerned about the most recent health threat to bees called Hive Collapse Disorder. The cause is UNKOWN. Doesn't that lead you to beleive that we should be very conservative at this time.  Take fewer risks with our biological food supply.  W
e can't unbreak this.
\par Please don't be as incompetent as the FDA.  They are often under fire lately because they have allowed unsafe drugs into our lives.  The reason they did this is because they took large risks and they were not willing to wait for the sc
ience to be done.  My word - they were incompetent.
\par You are carrying out important public business.  I expect you to protect my food supply.   I would really like to see the USDA working to prevent this kind of thing rather than enable it.  The smart futur
e is for smaller more organic farms with biodiverse approaches.  It is going to be hard enough to get through any coming climate change without adding horrors like those possible if this is allowed. 
\par 
\par I also can not beleive that the USDA would allow this to happen to normal farmers who may be held liable for any contamination. 
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether. Really take some serious thought here. Do Not Allow This. 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Debra Anderson
\par 106 Darling Street
\par Bennington, VT 05201
\par 
\par 
