\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in the tornado-prone midwest, where winds will easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring
 fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens low-income farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted
