\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   5:07 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Since you've been captured by the industry you regulate, I don't expect any action - but the responsible thing to do is ban this technology until the spread of inserted genes can be controlled.  
\par 
\par We don't need human genes passed from plant to plant, ending up in our food supply.  The FDA requires a prescription to obtain pharmaceutical products.  This technology will make pharmaceuticals nearly unavoidable.  I don't want hormones in my Wheaties.  

\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Jesse Wilson
\par 818 Cowper
\par 3
\par Palo Alto, CA 94301
\par 
\par 
