\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Growing 'Pharma' and industrial food crops outdoors invariable will contaminate crops meant for human consumption and, therefore, pose a risk to people. Kansas is a state where many tornados happen. Even with normal windforces, the seeds of tho
se plants that are meant to produce pharmaceuticals will be dispersed and pose a risk. Unfortunately it will be the farmer and not the USDA or the biotechnology company that planted the genetically engineered plants who will be held responsible for any da
mage to other crops or to humans.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
