\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 Gayle Janzen
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 11232 Dayton Ave N , Seattle, WA 98133 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   4:43 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Why the USDA is so determined to turn us all into guinea pigs is beyond me. It is impossible to contain these crops so that they don't contanimate neighboring fields. And then what happens?? No one knows. What are you g
oing to do if these crops cause neighboring crops to become sterile or kills off beneficial insects such as bees that are necessary to pollenate? Bees are vanishing at an alarming rate in the U.S and while no one knows for sure why at this time, one possi
b
le explanation is that genetically modified crops could be affecting them in a negative way. With global warming threatening to change the way we live, are you really ready to start experimenting with this unnecessary experiment when you don't even know t
h
e outcome??? Tried and true organic farming is the ONLY thing the USDA should be working to sustain and increase. It is the only way to keep people and the planet healthy and it's such a simple way of being. Please, quit doing Mother Nature's job - she's 
way better at it than any human who thnks they can one up her. 
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighbo
ring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to pre
vent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Gayle Janzen
\par 11232 Dayton Ave N
\par Seattle, WA 98133
\par 
\par 
