\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 Linda Lindgren
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 89 Juniper Hill , Francestown, NH 030433704 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   4:37 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Dear Fellow Human on Planet Earth!
\par 
\par Just say no to drug-producing rice. 
\par 
\par Why?
\par 
\par  IT'S COMPLETELY UNNECESSARY!  What "problem" are we trying to solve here?  
\par 
\par The potential "reward" is monetary and for the few, while the risk and potential "side effects" are borne, unwillingly, by the rest of us. 
\par 
\par I urge you to use your position in the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Put farming, our environment and public health ahead of the hubris and greed.
\par Stop it.  Now.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Linda Lindgren
\par 89 Juniper Hill
\par Francestown, NH 03043-3704
\par 
\par 
