\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   4:21 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food su
pply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be
 
held liable for contamination.  This poses a threat also to wildlife and contaminaton of the food chain from that angle.  Birds and other small grain eating animals that are part of the natural food chain could ingest the pharma crops and thus pollute hea
l
ty animals and inevitably humans.  Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination in that they have allowed cross contamination of natural eco systems from storms and other adverse weather condit
ions that can't be guarded against by open/outdoor farming of these pharma crops.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and geneticall engineered food crops and to institute a ban on this outdoor/open-air practice altogether. 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Stonewall Ogletree
\par 5652 Old Trappe Rd
\par Trappe, MD 21673-1938
\par 
\par 
