\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\fs20\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 Christopher Lauderdale
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 3118 Ostrom Ave. , Long Beach, CA 90808 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   4:06 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Stop growing drug-producing GE foods outdoors
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Anyone with an interest in GE foods knows the case of Percy Schmeister, the Canadian organic rapeseed farmer who was sued by Monsanto when his crop was "in
fected" by their GE rapeseed.  The Canadian Supreme Court sided with Monsanto, and the fallout has been damaging to independent farmers.  We also know about the contamination of heirloom strains of corn by GE corn in Mexico, thus damaging biodiversity.

\par 
\par "P
harma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in Kansas, where winds could easily blow Pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and 
threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Christopher Lauderdale
\par 3118 Ostrom Ave.
\par Long Beach, CA 90808
\par 
\par 
\par \page 
