\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par It doesn't take a tornado to produce winds hight enough to blow the seeds to neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat.  Just an wverage Kansas day could do it!  
\par 
\par Contamination of crops and streams pose potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.

\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban with appropriate audits and penalties on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Patricia Saucerman
\par 6020 Clare Road
\par Shawnee, KS 66226
