\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Please note that I live less than 15 miles from the proposed site, and am a faculty member at Kansas State University.  The fastest-growing segment of the KSU College of Agriculture is now Sustainable Ag--which opposes this kind 
of tinkering with our food supply.  I can find only one reason for approving this--corporate greed.   For the sake of future generations of both farmers and people, please do not approve this application.  Instead, do the right thing and create a policy t
hat bans this potentially disastrous farming practice.
\par 
\par Thank you,
\par 
\par David T. MacFarland 2030 Hunting Ave Manhattan, KS.  66502
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par David MacFarland
\par 2030 Hunting Ave
\par Manhattan, KS 66502
\par 
\par 
