\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   3:26 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial
 food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks
 to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Such contamination has happened before.Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I do not want to consume gen
etically engineered food products. If crops were contaminated by the wind, all of us could possibly consume such contaminated food products that have not been adaquately tested, nor found to be safe. There is a reason Europe forbids these products.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether. Puboic safety must be the first concern.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Sandra Carrubba
\par 200 East Hazeltine
\par Buffalo, NY 14217
\par 
\par 
