\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors-
-especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contam
ination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Why is the Dept. of Agriculture so pro pharma and industrial food crops?  Since food is a major concern for all citizens, why/how is this not something that should be reviewed/mandated in the House and Senate?
\par It all is getting pushed through too easily and smacks of favoritism, etc.  This area needs alot of investigation and policing. 
\par 
\par 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par louise bramhall
\par 1 cedar lane
\par gloucester, MA 01930
