\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   2:26 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par I am once again stunned by your caval
ier approach to genetically modified crops. These crops are pollution of the grossest kind, pollution with a life of it's own. Once out in the field, in nature, it spreads, just like any other plant does. These "pharma" and industrial food crops contamina
t
e food supplies (and already have): corn, soybeans, wheat and local family gardens. This contamination poses serious risks to human health, welfare and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Over and over again we have seen that neith
er the USDA (who seems to have been bought by companies like Monsanto) nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination. 
\par 
\par The job of the USDA is to first and foremost protect the citizens of this country, NOT corporations!!! Do your job 
and deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops. Immediately institute a ban on this hideous practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Bobbe Besold
\par 302 Lomita St
\par Santa Fe, NM 87505-8870
\par 
\par 
