\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors. Outdoor plantings are subject to weather which cannot be controlled, especially in Tornado Alley. Contamination poses potentially serious risk
s to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination. And once contamination occurs, it cannot be contained. Please do 
not let this genie out of its bottle.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Thank you for reading my letter.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Rose Jenkins
\par 1012 N High St
\par Duncannon, PA 17020-1812
