\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Genetic engineering of our food supply is a scary prospect no matter what the possible benefits are.  Many studies have already shown a building resistance of pests to GE food.  Bees have shown that they do not want to pollinate GE plants
.  Every third bite of food eaten in America is dependent on bees for their pollinating ability.  Also GE food has been shown to cross pollinate with wild species of similar plants.  This would lead to a food supply in which every time we eat we are getti
n
g unregulated doses of drugs that we do not need and in some cases could be harmful to the people that consume them.  Most infants are fed baby cereal that is rice based.   This would mean that infants, our most chemical susceptible population, would be r
e
ceiving unnecessary drugs. These are just some of the problems associated with genetically engineered food, and they are just the tip of the iceberg.  If we want to have a healthy food supply and a healthy nation please oppose and ban the use of all genet
ically engineered crops in our food supply.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Shane Zeman
\par 77 Avon Drive
\par Nashua, NH 03064
\par 
\par 
\par \page 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\fs20\insrsid7698630 
