\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds int
o neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that the USDA Restrictions and biotechnology companies cannot 
be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par Just look at the planting of a few acres of "superweeds" that went wrong. Winds blew the "superweed" pollen 9-10 miles outside of the test area borders !!!!  An outcropping of this magnatuitde CANNOT happen at all with 
biotech crops. I'm sure that there are other ways to grow those crops (like inside a biohazzard containment facility ), than to grow something that dangerous outdoors !!!! Just think for a moment what would happen if only a few outcroppings happened by te
s
t fields.....several farms or land would be contaminated, and those lands' pollen would spread to other lands' crops, and so on, and so on, until most everything would be permantely mixed with a pharmacrop. Eat corn and you may be eating corn+an Antibioti
c+who knows what else !!!!!
\par 
\par Based on the above, I strongly urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether. Remember, once the genie
 is out of the bottle it can't be put back in. 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Brian Angel
\par 15100 S. 94th Ave.
\par Orland Park, IL 60462
\par 
\par 
