\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: No genetically enginered foods - PLEASE
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par The rice contains human genes and would produce pharmaceutical substances. Drug-producing food crops grown outdoors pose risks to public health and the economic well-being of farmers because they are likely to contaminate the food supply. 
\par 
\par Please do what is the best for folks like me, error on the side of keeping our food safe and natural. The drug companies are already doing far too well at our health's expense.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Judith Knecht
\par 4817 Bowfield Drive
\par Antioch, TN 37013
\par 
\par 
