\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   1:13 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par It is apalling to me that you'd allow research and experimentation on "Pharma" and industrial food crops in an agricultural region where contamination could so easily occur.
\par Our food supply is BASIC to human health and the livelihood of our farmers. Until the issue of GE crops is decided to everyone's satisfaction, PLEASE don't allow our foods to be contaminated. I believe the potential for disturbance and disaster is great.

\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Judy Bogaerts
\par 4201 Linden Ln
\par Rolling Meadows, IL 60008
\par 
\par 
