\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par First the USDA allowed salmon genes to be placed into raspberries, supposedly to help prevent freezing in cold weather.
\par 
\par Now, the USDA has allowed the placement of human genes into rice (cannibalism by any other name) to supposedly help prevent childhood diarrhea.
\par 
\par Honeybee colonies throughout the United States are mysteriously dying.  Thousands of sheep and dozens of humans have mysteriously died in India while working around bT cotton fields.
\par 
\par How far will the USDA allow the world's food supply to be contaminated before it stops this insanity?
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Tony Rich
\par 59-1526 Kohala Ranch Road
\par Kamuela, HI 96743-8536
\par 
\par 
