\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   1:09 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into 
neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted
 to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par It is becoming increasingly difficult for Americans to raise their families with whole, pure foods in a clean environment. The risks involved if this type of crop is allowed is too great. We will already be combating the ill effe
cts of chemical treatment of our food crops for years. The risks were not understood at the onset of using pesticides, insectisides, chemical fertilizers. Americans health suffers, as well as the environment. America's wealth is also effected as outside c
ountries ban American grown products.
\par 
\par Please. Protect America and Americans. I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Lindee Adams
\par 1235 Kinghorn Rd
\par Pocatello, ID 83201
\par 
\par 
