\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are certain to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors. This is especially a problem in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds would blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat.
\par 
\par Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health, and threatens the security of farmers, who may be held liable for contamination of their 
own un-engineered crops. Contamination is inevitable, and it would be both naive and unrealistic to think it can be avoided or prevented.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crop,s and to institute a complete ban on this irresponsible practice.
\par 
\par Sincerely, Ravenna Taylor 43 Lambert Road Stockton, New Jersey 08559
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Ravenna Taylor
\par 43 Lambert Road
\par Stockton, NJ 08559
\par 
