\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par As a scientist, I find it unthinkable that the USDA does not recognize the serious risks to our food supply and to human health that outdoor drug production presents.  The contamination of other crops is inevitabl
e, particularly from a project of this scale and in an area subject to severe weather.   
\par 
\par I strongly urge a denial of this application and the enactment of a total ban on the outdoor growing of all pharmaceutical and industrial crops.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Cheryl Gross
\par 4086 Tern Street
\par Sarasota, FL 34232
\par 
