\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 1446 Auction Road , Manheim, PA 17545 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 8, 2007   1:07 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easi
ly blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotech
nology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par While all caution shou
ld be used with genetically engineered crops, special care should be taken with wind pollinated genetically engineered crops.  It is impossible to contain wind borne pollen within an open field, and with high winds pollen could be carried hundreds of mile
s to contaminate other fields.  Putting these crops in an open field is a foolhardy endeavor.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Jo Anna Hebberger
\par 1446 Auction Road
\par Manheim, PA 17545
\par 
\par 
