\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could eas
ily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotec
hnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par P. S. As a former res
earcher and farmer I feel that bio-engeneering is moving too fast. Mistakes have been made in the past that could have been prevented had more time been allowed for more study. We are now working in an area that has not been totaly proven to not have adve
rse effect in and on many parts of the biological world. Please move in the area of caution. E.F.S.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Erwin Sawall Jr.
\par 3351 Holland Loop Road
\par Cave Junction, OR 97523
