\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors-
-especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contam
ination. Experience shows that neither good intentions or biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par Studies have shown that natural pollinators preferentially choose organic  crops.  They also AVOID genetically engineered crops.  What do they know that we as humans can't detect with our limited senses?  I vote to go with the pollinator's warning to us!

\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Sue Rau
\par 178 Fayette Road
\par Massena, NY 13662
