\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Pharmaceudical and industrial food crops are likely to c
ontaminate the food supply if grown outdoors. In tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat and contaminate them. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health 
