\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow ph
arma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology com
panies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Please start concentrating on ho
w we can help farmers produce more "natural" crops of food, (as God gave us), and quit trying to ALTAR our most precious resource in the name of progress!  We do not know what horrors this will present down the line, and our money could be used toward hig
her production and dissemination of products instead of experimentation!  Let's get the job done as it was orignally meant to be!  START LISTENING TO THE PEOPLE OF THIS COUNTRY, PLEASE!!!!
\par 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Jacqueline Schroller
