\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par No one asked me if I wanted "Pharma" and industrial food crops and if you did I would say "NO."  As you well know, they are likely to contaminate the foo
d supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who ma
y be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par The USDA is not a sanctioned medical health care provider to America and should not tamper with our lives throug
h the food supply.  I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely, Alicia Berger 6974 Calle Del Paz West Boca Raton, FL 33433
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Alicia Berger
\par 6974 Calle Del Paz W.
\par Boca Raton, FL 33433
\par 
