\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops
 are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human h
ealth and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production
 of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether. With future demands for healthy foods for human consumption as worldwide populations increase, we don't need to endanger that supply by using plants to provid
e pharmaceuticals or fuels.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Fred Reinman
\par 540 3rd Court
\par Fox Island, WA 98333
