\par Subject: Preserve life, preserve integrity: please keep drugs out of our food supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par I should point that I am Brazilian, an
d in my country we are facing the same battle against non-tested transgenic crops. Do not let this happen in your country, too. Remember it will be seen as a good action, which will help to improve The United States image to the World.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and indust
rial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious r
isks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Ivan Linares
\par Rua Padre Landim, 292-- Ap. 804 -- Torre
\par -- Ap. 804 -- Torre -- CEP 50.710-470
\par Recife -- Pernambuco -- Brazil, NY 10093
