\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 christine hoex
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 300 horn ave , santa rosa, CA 95407 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 26, 2007   5:27 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par Please for the sake of our children, and the future of safe food, read this message that I am sending.
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are highly likely to contaminate the food supply i
f grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. We do not have controll of the elements, and it's not fair to include all consumers as guinea pigs j
u
st because the biotech industry is profit driven and can't be relied on to do the careful contained research that this science demands. Biotech can hold many positive results for our future, but we are in danger of losing that future if we let pharma crop
s
 get out of controll. Remember Rachael Carsons SILLENT SPRING. There are always unforeseen consequences. Contamination is a serious risk to human health, ours and our children. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trus
ted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether. 
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par christine hoex
\par 300 horn ave
\par santa rosa, CA 95407
\par 
\par 
