\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\fs20\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 Katherine Chess
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\brdrt\brdrs\brdrw60\brsp20 \wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\rtlgutter\itap0 {\f36\fs22\insrsid7698630 914 Seahorse Court , Ventura, CA 93001 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \qr \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\insrsid7698630 March 26, 2007   5:27 PM}{\b\f36\fs32\insrsid7698630 
\par }\pard \ql \li0\ri0\nowidctlpar\wrapdefault\faauto\rin0\lin0\itap0 {\f36\insrsid7698630 
\par Secretary Mike Johanns
\par Secretary of Agriculture
\par U.S. Department of Agriculture
\par  
\par 
\par Subject: Keep Drugs Out of Our Food Supply!
\par 
\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par As a Biologist and Botanist, I fear the potential ramifications of using Any genetically modified organisms for food or medicine. This concern is directed toward human health as well as health of domestic animals and natural ecosystems. 
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if
 grown outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held l
iable for contamination. Experience shows that neither the USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination.
\par 
\par We do not know enough yet to allow mixing genetically modified crops into open agriculture. As a scientist, I think it is a
 short-sighted, ignorant decision to allow this direction with genetic research. Natural systems are already challenged too much by humans. We should Not introduce potentially dangerous (even disasterous) modified oganisms into agricultural or natural lan
ds. 
\par 
\par I urge the USDA to deny this and all other applications for outdoor production of pharmaceutical and industrial food crops and to institute a ban on this practice altogether.
\par 
\par Sincerely,
\par Katherine Chess
\par 914 Seahorse Court
\par Ventura, CA 93001
\par 
\par 
