\par 
\par Dear Secretary Johanns,
\par 
\par I am writing to urge the U.S. Department of Agriculture (USDA) to deny the application by Ventria Bioscience to grow up to 3,200 acres of genetically engineered, drug-producing rice in Kansas.
\par 
\par "Pharma" and industrial food crops are likely to contaminate the food supply if grown
 outdoors--especially in tornado-prone Kansas, where winds could easily blow pharma rice seeds into neighboring fields of corn, soybeans, or wheat. Contamination poses potentially serious risks to human health and threatens farmers who may be held liable 
for contamination. Experience shows that NEITHER THE USDA nor biotechnology companies can be trusted to prevent contamination. I'D LIKE YOU TO BE MORE CONCERNED ABOUT THE PUBLIC HEALTH THAN ABOUT THE GENETIC ENGINEERING COMPANIES AND THEIR PROFITS.
